invariant: INV-22
file: tls.c
catches: unit
reason: ch_read reads the record the peer sent after its close_notify,
  where RFC 9846 section 6.1 says data after a closure alert MUST be
  ignored. It takes the bytes from the transport and fails the session
  on them, so a peer that closed cleanly ends this side's session.

--- old
    if (t->read_closed) {
        return 0; // the peer's close_notify arrived; nothing after it is read
    }
--- new
